### Reviews API Documentation
### Complete API documentation for reviews management endpoints
### All operations for creating, updating, and retrieving reviews

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@contentType = application/json
@token = your-jwt-token-here
@reviewId = your-review-uuid-here
@userId = your-user-uuid-here
@projectId = your-project-uuid-here
@contractId = your-contract-uuid-here

### ============================================
### VARIABLES SETUP
### ============================================
### Replace the variables above with actual values:
### - @token: JWT token from /api/auth/verify-otp
### - @reviewId: UUID of an existing review
### - @userId: UUID of a user (for getting reviews by user)
### - @projectId: UUID of a project (for getting reviews by project)
### - @contractId: UUID of a contract (required for creating reviews)

### ============================================
### 1. CREATE REVIEW
### ============================================
### Create a new review for a completed project/contract
### Requires authentication (user token)
### All ratings must be integers between 1 and 5
### Required fields: projectId, contractId, userId, review, and all rating fields

POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "projectId": "f8c46c12-3636-4191-b114-61b9343c1d39",
  "contractId": "b7fa214c-6fd7-430b-a2af-3f390668f39e",
  "userId": "eef045d7-71cd-423c-9b39-8d22b29ded0f",
  "review": "Excellent work! The freelancer delivered high-quality work on time and communicated effectively throughout the project.",
  "proffeciency": 5,
  "communication": 5,
  "quality": 5,
  "experience": 4,
  "onTimeDelivery": 5,
  "willHireAgain": 5
}

### Example: Create Review with Lower Ratings
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "projectId": "f8c46c12-3636-4191-b114-61b9343c1d39",
  "contractId": "b7fa214c-6fd7-430b-a2af-3f390668f39e",
  "userId": "eef045d7-71cd-423c-9b39-8d22b29ded0f",
  "review": "Good work overall, but there were some communication delays.",
  "proffeciency": 4,
  "communication": 3,
  "quality": 4,
  "experience": 4,
  "onTimeDelivery": 4,
  "willHireAgain": 4
}

### ============================================
### 2. UPDATE/EDIT REVIEW
### ============================================
### Update an existing review (requires authentication)
### Only the user who created the review can update it
### At least one field must be provided for update
### All rating fields are optional and must be integers between 1 and 5

PATCH {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "review": "Updated review text - The work was even better than expected!",
  "proffeciency": 5,
  "communication": 5
}

### Example: Update Only Review Text
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "review": "After further consideration, I want to add that the freelancer was very professional and responsive."
}

### Example: Update Only Ratings
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "proffeciency": 5,
  "communication": 5,
  "quality": 5,
  "experience": 5,
  "onTimeDelivery": 5,
  "willHireAgain": 5
}

### ============================================
### 3. GET REVIEWS BY USER ID
### ============================================
### Get all reviews for a specific user
### Public endpoint (no authentication required)
### Returns all reviews where the user was reviewed

GET {{baseUrl}}/reviews/user/{{userId}}

### Example Response:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Reviews fetched successfully",
###   "data": [
###     {
###       "id": "review-uuid",
###       "projectId": "project-uuid",
###       "contractId": "contract-uuid",
###       "userId": "user-uuid",
###       "review": "Great work!",
###       "proffeciency": 5,
###       "communication": 5,
###       "quality": 5,
###       "experience": 4,
###       "onTimeDelivery": 5,
###       "willHireAgain": 5,
###       "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###       "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z"
###     }
###   ]
### }

### ============================================
### 4. GET REVIEWS BY PROJECT ID
### ============================================
### Get all reviews for a specific project
### Public endpoint (no authentication required)
### Returns all reviews associated with the project

GET {{baseUrl}}/reviews/project/{{projectId}}

### Example Response:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Reviews fetched successfully",
###   "data": [
###     {
###       "id": "review-uuid",
###       "projectId": "project-uuid",
###       "contractId": "contract-uuid",
###       "userId": "user-uuid",
###       "review": "Excellent work!",
###       "proffeciency": 5,
###       "communication": 5,
###       "quality": 5,
###       "experience": 5,
###       "onTimeDelivery": 5,
###       "willHireAgain": 5,
###       "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###       "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z"
###     }
###   ]
### }

### ============================================
### COMPREHENSIVE NOTES & GUIDELINES
### ============================================

### 1. AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION
###    - Create and Update endpoints require JWT token
###    - Format: Authorization: Bearer <token>
###    - Get token from: POST /api/auth/verify-otp
###    
###    Public endpoints (no auth required):
###    - GET /api/reviews/user/:userid (get reviews by user)
###    - GET /api/reviews/project/:project (get reviews by project)
###    
###    Authenticated endpoints:
###    - POST /api/reviews (create review)
###    - PATCH /api/reviews/:id (update review - only by creator)

### 2. RATING SYSTEM
###    - All ratings must be integers between 1 and 5
###    - Rating fields:
###      * proffeciency: Technical skills and expertise (1-5)
###      * communication: Communication quality (1-5)
###      * quality: Work quality (1-5)
###      * experience: Overall experience (1-5)
###      * onTimeDelivery: Punctuality (1-5)
###      * willHireAgain: Likelihood to hire again (1-5)
###    
###    Example ratings:
###    - 5: Excellent
###    - 4: Very Good
###    - 3: Good
###    - 2: Fair
###    - 1: Poor

### 3. VALIDATION RULES
###    Create Review:
###    - projectId: Required, must be valid UUID
###    - contractId: Required, must be valid UUID
###    - userId: Required, must be valid UUID (user being reviewed)
###    - review: Required, non-empty string
###    - All rating fields: Required, integer 1-5
###    
###    Update Review:
###    - At least one field must be provided
###    - review: Optional, non-empty string if provided
###    - All rating fields: Optional, integer 1-5 if provided

### 4. ERROR RESPONSES
###    
###    Validation Error (400):
###    {
###      "success": false,
###      "message": "Validation error message",
###      "errors": [
###        {
###          "field": "proffeciency",
###          "message": "Rating must be at most 5"
###        }
###      ]
###    }
###    
###    Unauthorized (401):
###    {
###      "success": false,
###      "message": "Unauthorized"
###    }
###    
###    Not Found (404):
###    {
###      "success": false,
###      "message": "Review not found"
###    }
###    
###    Forbidden (403):
###    {
###      "success": false,
###      "message": "You are not authorized to update this review"
###    }

### 5. SUCCESS RESPONSES
###    
###    Create Review (201):
###    {
###      "success": true,
###      "message": "Review created successfully",
###      "data": {
###        "id": "review-uuid",
###        "projectId": "project-uuid",
###        "contractId": "contract-uuid",
###        "userId": "user-uuid",
###        "review": "Review text",
###        "proffeciency": 5,
###        "communication": 5,
###        "quality": 5,
###        "experience": 4,
###        "onTimeDelivery": 5,
###        "willHireAgain": 5,
###        "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###        "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z"
###      }
###    }
###    
###    Update Review (200):
###    {
###      "success": true,
###      "message": "Review updated successfully",
###      "data": {
###        "id": "review-uuid",
###        ... (updated fields)
###      }
###    }
###    
###    Get Reviews (200):
###    {
###      "success": true,
###      "message": "Reviews fetched successfully",
###      "data": [
###        ... (array of review objects)
###      ]
###    }

### 6. BEST PRACTICES
###    - Create reviews only after project completion
###    - Be honest and constructive in review text
###    - Rate all categories fairly
###    - Update reviews if circumstances change
###    - Use reviews to help other users make informed decisions

### 7. COMMON USE CASES
###    
###    Case 1: Client reviews freelancer after project completion
###    1. Project is completed
###    2. Client creates review via POST /api/reviews
###    3. Review is associated with project, contract, and freelancer (userId)
###    
###    Case 2: View freelancer's review history
###    1. Get all reviews for a freelancer: GET /api/reviews/user/:userid
###    2. Calculate average ratings from all reviews
###    
###    Case 3: View project reviews
###    1. Get all reviews for a project: GET /api/reviews/project/:project
###    2. Display reviews to help future clients make decisions
###    
###    Case 4: Update review after reflection
###    1. User realizes they were too harsh/lenient
###    2. Update review via PATCH /api/reviews/:id
###    3. Only the creator can update their review

### ============================================
### TESTING EXAMPLES
### ============================================

### Test: Create Review with All Maximum Ratings
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "projectId": "{{projectId}}",
  "contractId": "{{contractId}}",
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "review": "Outstanding work in every aspect! Highly recommended.",
  "proffeciency": 5,
  "communication": 5,
  "quality": 5,
  "experience": 5,
  "onTimeDelivery": 5,
  "willHireAgain": 5
}

### Test: Create Review with Minimum Ratings
POST {{baseUrl}}/reviews
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "projectId": "{{projectId}}",
  "contractId": "{{contractId}}",
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "review": "Needs improvement in several areas.",
  "proffeciency": 1,
  "communication": 1,
  "quality": 1,
  "experience": 1,
  "onTimeDelivery": 1,
  "willHireAgain": 1
}

### Test: Update Review - Improve Ratings
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "proffeciency": 5,
  "communication": 5,
  "quality": 5,
  "experience": 5,
  "onTimeDelivery": 5,
  "willHireAgain": 5
}

### Test: Update Review - Add More Detail
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "review": "After working together more, I can confirm this freelancer is exceptional. They went above and beyond expectations, delivered ahead of schedule, and maintained excellent communication throughout. I would definitely hire again!"
}
